            "content": ", where "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "b"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " is a real number  \nprediction equation (38) an equation suggested by the points of a scatter plot used to predict other points  \npre-image (88) the graph of an object before a transformation  \nprincipal values (406, 456) the unique solutions of a trigonometric equation if the values of the function are restricted to two adjacent quadrants  \nprisoner point (816) If the iterates do not approach infinity for some initial value, that point is called a prisoner point.  \nprisoner set (599) the set of initial values for which the iterates of a function do not approach infinity  \nprobability (852) the measure of the chance of a desired outcome happening  \npure imaginary number (206, 581) the complex number "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "a + bi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " when "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "a = 0"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "b \\neq 0"
          }
