        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "rational inequality (245) an inequality that consists of one or more rational expressions  \nratio test (785) a method to test convergence in an infinite series  \nreal part of a complex number (581) "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "a"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " in the complex number "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "a + bi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "  \nrectangular form (581) a complex number written as "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "x + yi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": ", where "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "x"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " is the real part and "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "yi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " is the imaginary part  \nrectangular hyperbola (648) A special case of the equilateral hyperbola, where the coordinate axes are the asymptotes. The general equation of a rectangular hyperbola is "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "xy = c"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": ", where "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "c"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " is a nonzero constant.  \nrecursive formula (758) a formula used for determining the next term of a sequence using one or more of the previous terms  \nreduced sample space (862) the subset of a sample space that contains only those outcomes that satisfy a given condition  \nreduction identity (446) identity that involves adding and subtracting the quandrantal angles, "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "90^\\circ"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": ", "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "180^\\circ"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": ", and "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "270^\\circ"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": ", from the angle measure to find equivalent values of a trigonometric function  \nreference angle (280) the acute angle formed by the terminal side of an angle in standard position and the "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "x"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "-axis  \nreflection (88) a linear transformation that flips a figure over a line called the line of symmetry  \nreflection matrix (89) a matrix used to reflect an object over a line or plane  \nregression line (40) a best-fit line  \nrelation (5) a set of ordered pairs  \nrelative extremum (172) a point that represents the maximum or minimum for a certain interval  \nrelative maximum (172) a point that represents the maximum for a certain interval  \nrelative minimum (172) a point that represents the minimum for a certain interval  \nresultant of vectors (486) the sum of two or more vectors  \nroot (206) a solution of the equation "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "P(x) = 0"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "  \nrose (563) The graph of a polar equation of the form "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "r = a \\cos n\\theta"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " or "
          },
          {
            "type": "equation_inline",
            "content": "r = a \\sin n\\theta"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": ".  \nrotation (88) a transformation in which an object is moved around a center point  \nrotation matrix (91) a matrix used to rotate an object  \nrow matrix (78) a matrix that has only one row"
          }
        ],
